  "name": "Panda Route (A350 fleet)",
  "kind": "standard",
  "from": "2018",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "drawnOn": "A359",
  "description": "Sichuan Airlines' A350-900s all wear the 'Panda Route' art scheme: a white forward fuselage with a big cartoon giant panda lying among broad leaves (blue, green, yellow, navy), a fan of pink, yellow, blue and green leaves under the titles, then a sweep from light orange through orange to red behind the wing, the red aft fuselage scattered with more leaves (yellow, blue, purple, green), small pandas and ribbons. Blue '四川航空' and 'SICHUAN AIRLINES' over the windows ahead of the wing, white 'PANDA ROUTE' aft. Red fin with Sichuan's white disc (a blue seagull over waves); red winglets; white engines. Drawn simplified: the big leaves and colour sweep as areas, the pandas as logo entries, small figures left out.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B-32G6_at_CTU_T1_20260810145032.jpg",
      "title": "B-32G6 at CTU T1 20260810145032.jpg (CC BY-SA 4.0, TurnOnTheNight)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-20",
      "note": "A350-900 B-32G6, right side, parked at Chengdu Tianfu, 2026-08-10. Flipped and fitted to shapes/A359.json (doors 1 and 4 pinned; ~20 px off at door 4 and the fin root, as the 787 fits were): the colour sweep, leaves, titles, fin disc."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B-32G6@PEK_(20250608154417).jpg",
      "title": "B-32G6@PEK (20250608154417).jpg (CC BY-SA 4.0, N509FZ)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-20",
      "note": "B-32G6, left side from below on approach to Beijing, 2025-06-08: the left side's art (same layout, panda posed differently), titles, red winglets; too foreshortened to fit (the fit was 25 px off at both doors)."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B-325J@PEK_(20240123140138).jpg",
      "title": "B-325J@PEK (20240123140138).jpg (CC BY-SA 4.0, N509FZ)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-20",
      "note": "A350-900 B-325J (the LAX flight's aircraft on 2026-11-20, per ADS-B), left side banking on approach, 2024-01-23: the same scheme on the LAX airframe."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Current_Airbus_A350-900_of_Sichuan_Airlines",
      "title": "Category:Current Airbus A350-900 of Sichuan Airlines (Wikimedia Commons)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-20",
      "note": "All six A350-900s with photos (B-306N, B-325J, B-32AG, B-32F8, B-32G2, B-32G6, 2019-2026) wear this scheme."
    }
