  "notes": "The Panda Route ('熊猫之路') scheme is on every Sichuan A350-900 photographed (2019-2026); the LAX service (CSC3837/3838, Chengdu Tianfu-LAX, weekly) is flown by these A350s (B-325J on 2026-11-20). Sichuan's A320s and A330s wear its ordinary white scheme with the red fin, not drawn here: no other type is seen at LAX. It's an art scheme drawn simplified: 19 fuselage areas (the white-to-red sweep in three steps at x 0.46/0.54/0.605, and 16 of the biggest leaves), the pandas as logo entries; the small pandas, ribbons, musical notes and the faint orange leaf aft of the wing are left out. Measured on B-32G6's right side (2026-08-10); the left side's art has the same layout (panda forward between doors 1 and 2, leaf fan under the titles, leaves behind the wing) but differs in detail, and couldn't be fitted from the 2025 photo (strong foreshortening): the areas are drawn on both sides from the right side's measure, and the left side's leaves are only roughly where they are drawn. The real sweep is a smooth gradient. The belly isn't seen.",
  "history": "New in the LAX round 2 (2026-11-20); CSC had no scheme here before."
}
